# Cursor Rules for CV and Motivation Letter Generation

## CV and Motivation Letter Generation Process

When the user asks to generate a CV and/or motivation letter for a job application:

1. **Locate the job description**: The job description should be at `professional/CV/Job Descriptions/[job title]/Description.txt`. If the user provides a job description path or mentions a job title, use that location.

2. **Read required files**:

   - Read the job description from `professional/CV/Job Descriptions/[job title]/Description.txt`
   - Read `professional/CV/cv_format_spec.md` to understand the format requirements
   - Read `README.md` from the repository root as the source of truth for all experiences, projects, achievements, and skills

3. **Generate cv.txt**:

   - Create `professional/CV/Job Descriptions/[job title]/cv.txt` in the same directory as the job description
   - Follow the format specified in `professional/CV/cv_format_spec.md`:
     - **Intro Section**: Opening line with title/role tags, 2 paragraphs about professional identity, optional key achievements. Must be between 570 and 580 characters in length (excluding project links in parentheses). Use real, flowing sentences, not fragmented bullet-style text.
     - **Skills Section**: Technical skills (Techniques) and project/process skills (Projet) relevant to the job description, selected from README.md. Format: "Techniques: [comma-separated list]" and "Projet: [comma-separated list]". The language should match the job description language.
     - **Job Experiences Section**: Maximum 3 job experiences selected from README.md "Professional Experience" section **based on relevance to the job description**. **Experiences must always be listed in reverse chronological order (most recent first)**. Each with:
       - `[ICON]` Company/Project Name - Role Title (use `[ICON]` placeholder instead of markdown links)
       - Date Range (e.g., "Dec. 2022 – Present")
       - 2-3 bullet points written as plain text sentences without bullet markers (no "-" prefix). Each bullet point must be a complete, real sentence (not fragmented bullet-style text). Bullet points should start with past participles (e.g., "Développé", "Créé", "Implémenté") rather than using "Je" or "J'ai". Each bullet point should be approximately 75 characters in length (excluding project links in parentheses).
       - When mentioning specific projects, include project link(s) in parentheses immediately after the project name: `ProjectName (https://url.com)`. Priority order for links: website > PyPI > GitHub. Only one link per project in intro section.
     - **Links Section**: After the job experiences section, include a "Links" subsection listing all URLs in the format: `Project/Company Name: https://url.com`
     - **More Info Section**: Technical stack (grouped by Backend/Frontend/Database/DevOps), Education, Languages, Open to opportunities

4. **Generate motivation_letter.txt**:

   - Create `professional/CV/Job Descriptions/[job title]/motivation_letter.txt` in the same directory as the job description
   - Follow the 4-paragraph structure from `professional/CV/cv_format_spec.md`:
     - **Paragraph 1**: Opening & Interest - express genuine interest, mention discovery, align with career goals
     - **Paragraph 2**: Relevant Experience & Skills - reference 2-3 key requirements from job description, connect to README experiences, highlight matching technical skills, include metrics
     - **Paragraph 3**: Cultural Fit & Values - reference impact areas from README, show alignment with company values, mention relevant soft skills
     - **Paragraph 4**: Closing - reiterate enthusiasm, express willingness to discuss, professional closing
   - Must be tailored to the specific job description
   - Must reference specific requirements from the job description
   - Must connect experiences from README.md to job requirements
   - Length: 3-4 paragraphs, concise and focused
   - Tone: Professional, enthusiastic, authentic

5. **Validation step** - After generating cv.txt:

   - Verify that all bullet points in the job experiences section are approximately 75 characters in length (excluding project links in parentheses)
   - Verify that the intro section is between 570 and 580 characters in length (excluding all project links in parentheses) and consists of 2 paragraphs
   - Adjust any bullet points or intro section that do not meet these requirements

6. **Key principles**:

   - All content must be based on information from README.md
   - Job experiences must be selected from README.md "Professional Experience" section (max 3) **based on relevance to the job description requirements**
   - Job experiences must always be listed in reverse chronological order (most recent first)
   - Always include metrics/quantifiable results when available
   - Use `[ICON]` placeholder instead of markdown links in the text
   - List all links separately after the relevant section in the format: `Project/Company Name: https://url.com`
   - Tailor content to match job description requirements
   - Use professional, authentic language
   - Avoid overusing the words "expert" or "expertise". Use alternative phrasing such as "experienced in", "skilled in", "proficient with", or describe specific achievements and capabilities instead.
   - **Phrasing for job experience bullet points**: Write complete, natural sentences that start with past participles (e.g., "Développé", "Créé", "Implémenté", "Contribué", "Collaboré"). Do not use "Je" or "J'ai" at the beginning of bullet points. Ensure sentences are real, flowing formulations, not fragmented bullet-style text.
   - The output language (for both cv.txt and motivation_letter.txt) must match the language of the job description. If the job description is in French, output in French. If in English, output in English.

7. **Output**: Both files should be created in `professional/CV/Job Descriptions/[job title]/` directory alongside the job description.
